    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "2TI",
      "chapter": 3,
      "chapter_usfm": "2TI.3",
      "version_id": 3034,
      "version_abbr": "BSB",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But understand this: In the last days terrible times will come."
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For men will be lovers of themselves, lovers of money, boastful, arrogant, abusive, disobedient to their parents, ungrateful, unholy,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "unloving, unforgiving, slanderous, without self-control, brutal, without love of good,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.4",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "traitorous, reckless, conceited, lovers of pleasure rather than lovers of God,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.5",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "having a form of godliness but denying its power. Turn away from such as these!"
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "They are the kind who worm their way into households and captivate vulnerable women who are weighed down with sins and led astray by various passions,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "who are always learning but never able to come to a knowledge of the truth."
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Just as Jannes and Jambres opposed Moses, so also these men oppose the truth. They are depraved in mind and disqualified from the faith."
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But they will not advance much further. For just like Jannes and Jambres, their folly will be plain to everyone."
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.10",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "You, however, have observed my teaching, my conduct, my purpose, my faith, my patience, my love, my perseverance,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.11",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "my persecutions, and the sufferings that came upon me in Antioch, Iconium, and Lystra. What persecutions I endured! Yet the Lord rescued me from all of them."
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.12",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Indeed, all who desire to live godly lives in Christ Jesus will be persecuted,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.13",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "while evil men and imposters go from bad to worse, deceiving and being deceived."
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.14",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But as for you, continue in the things you have learned and firmly believed, since you know from whom you have learned them."
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.15",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "From infancy you have known the Holy Scriptures, which are able to make you wise for salvation through faith in Christ Jesus."
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.16",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "All Scripture is God-breathed and is useful for instruction, for conviction, for correction, and for training in righteousness,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 17,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.17",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "so that the man of God may be complete, fully equipped for every good work."
        }
      ],
      "verse_count": 17,
      "headings": [
        {
          "before_verse": 10,
          "text": "All Scripture Is God-Breathed"
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "2TI.3.8",
          "note_ref": "3:8",
          "note_type": "footnote",
          "references": [],
          "text": "See Jasher 79:27. The Book of Jashar or the Book of the Upright One is often cited as Jasher."
        }
      ],
